WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.523 --> 00:00:17.544
doesn't the princess have gravity?"

2
00:00:18.264 --> 00:00:20.005
The king paced back and forth.

3
00:00:20.025 --> 00:00:23.527
"My queen, this child can't be ours.

4
00:00:24.748 --> 00:00:28.130
Someone took our baby and gave us this light one instead!"

5
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.872
"Don't be silly, dear," the queen said.

6
00:00:32.656 --> 00:00:35.237
"I think something else caused this problem."

7
00:00:35.257 --> 00:00:37.257
"What do you mean?"

8
00:00:37.557 --> 00:00:38.298
the king asked.

9
00:00:38.318 --> 00:00:42.199
"We didn't watch Ellen carefully at the baptism.

10
00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:45.179
And The queen cleared her throat.

11
00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.541
"Someone who was not invited got too close to her."

12
00:00:59.763 --> 00:01:01.944
"Aha!" The king slapped his forehead.

13
00:01:02.736 --> 00:01:03.356
"I get it.

14
00:01:03.817 --> 00:01:06.298
My sister put a spell on her!"

15
00:01:06.318 --> 00:01:10.120
"Exactly," the queen said sadly.

16
00:01:12.941 --> 00:01:15.802
Everyone did their best to watch the baby princess.

17
00:01:16.182 --> 00:01:17.903
But accidents kept happening.

18
00:01:18.764 --> 00:01:23.286
For example, one fine summer day, Nanny put her to sleep.

19
00:01:24.446 --> 00:01:27.248
She covered the princess with a blanket to hold her down.

20
00:01:33.224 --> 00:01:34.766
Later the queen entered the room.

21
00:01:35.766 --> 00:01:37.508
She didn't see the sleeping baby.

22
00:01:37.528 --> 00:01:40.110
"What a nice day!"

23
00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.271
the queen said.

24
00:01:41.291 --> 00:01:43.653
"I'll let in some fresh air."

25
00:01:44.754 --> 00:01:46.816
She opened a window and then hurried off.

26
00:01:47.877 --> 00:01:51.940
She didn't realize a magical fairy wind was blowing outside.

27
00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:56.064
It swirled around the window, waiting to do some mischief.

28
00:01:56.984 --> 00:02:00.607
As soon as the queen left, the fairy wind rushed in.

29
00:02:01.147 --> 00:02:04.149
It danced over to the bed and swept up Ellen.

30
00:02:10.274 --> 00:02:12.456
Then it blew back outside.

31
00:02:13.997 --> 00:02:18.580
The small baby floated on the breeze like a tiny flower seed.

32
00:02:21.062 --> 00:02:23.744
When Nanny returned, the baby was gone!

33
00:02:27.208 --> 00:02:28.970
Nanny tried to stay calm.

34
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.372
"The queen probably took her," she thought.

35
00:02:33.073 --> 00:02:34.494
She ran to the queen's room.

36
00:02:34.514 --> 00:02:39.138
"Your Majesty, do you have Princess Ellen?"

37
00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:43.081
"No." The queen went pale.

38
00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:44.563
"Is she missing?"

39
00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:49.647
"I'm afraid so," Nanny said.

40
00:02:51.108 --> 00:02:53.190
The queen yelled for help.

41
00:02:53.951 --> 00:02:58.486
A moment later the palace was as busy as a beehive.

42
00:02:58.926 --> 00:03:01.747
Everyone buzzed about, searching for the missing baby.

43
00:03:15.956 --> 00:03:17.456
Finally a shout rang out.

44
00:03:17.476 --> 00:03:19.377
"I found her!"

45
00:03:19.818 --> 00:03:20.838
a servant cried.

46
00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:23.480
Everyone ran out to the garden.

47
00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:27.842
The baby lay under a rosebush, sound asleep.

48
00:03:28.503 --> 00:03:30.924
A thick blanket of rose petals covered her.

49
00:03:31.745 --> 00:03:34.146
The king and queen sobbed with relief.

50
00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.992
The noise woke up Ellen, who laughed and laughed.

51
00:03:45.213 --> 00:03:49.396
She kicked her tiny feet, spraying rose petals everywhere.
